# P18-V01 ProcessTimer clone identity and current-revision gate — 2026-10-17T15:20:44Z

- Repository: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`.
- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 commit
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; inspected read-only.
- Source review found Rust cloned `ProcessTimer` by value in command/hook
  snapshots and in the asynchronous response-write metric path. Java stores a
  Guava `Stopwatch` reference on `RemotingCommand`; processor and write
  callbacks continue to read that same mutable object. Rust now stores timer
  state behind `Arc<Mutex<_>>`, so cloned timer handles share start/stop/reset
  mutations. Public `&mut` method receivers and structural identity behavior
  remain intact.
- Added `cloned_process_timer_shares_java_stopwatch_state` to verify visible
  start/stop/reset behavior across clones. Code commit:
  `56ca072f fix(remoting): share process timer state across clones`.
- Documentation updates record the clone identity contract in
  `docs/compatibility/PHASE_6_API_CONFIG_MAP.md` and the current gate in
  `docs/release-checklist.md`.

